S3AHOME V1.4 - READ.ME file
----------------------------

Welcome to my Home Inventory program V1.4.  Please note this file is for New 
Users only.  Users upgrading from V1.3 should read README.V13

The archive should contain the following files:

S3AHOME4.APP        Main program

S3AHOMEH.OVL        Optional Help file
S3AHOMEP.OVL        Optional Print file
S3APRINT.DYL        Optional Print file

README.NEW          'Get you started' instructions for new users
README.V13          Upgrade instructions for present users of V1.3

HISTORY.TXT         Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

REGISTER.TXT        Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT         A legal document

S3AHOME4.DOC        Full instructions in Word format
S3AHOME4.TXT        Full instructions in ASCII Text format

I would strongly encourage you to read the instructions, but
if you still insist on flying blind:

     1.   Put S3AHOME4.APP in your \APP\ directory

     2.   If you want to use the optional On-Line Help (Highly recommended)
          put the file S3AHOMEH.OVL into an \APP\S3AHOME\ directory.

     3.   If you want to use the optional Print option put the file 
          S3AHOMEP.OVL into the \APP\S3AHOME\ directory and the file
          S3APRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  Note that this file is
          common to all my programs, so if you have more than one of
          them you only need one copy of this file.

     4.   Install (PSION-I) and go for it !!

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions.  I have yet to 
be asked a question that wasn't already fully explained in the instructions !!

All comments, and registrations, still gratefully received.

If you wish to register, up-to-date details are in the file REGISTER.TXT

If you want to monitor progress on upgrades and enhancements, as well as see if 
any bugs have been reported, visit my home page on the World-Wide Web. The address is :  

http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/alanrichey

If you like the look of the program you may also like to check out my other programs:

